      "overview": "## Lesson Overview\n\nClient–server communication is the backbone of every web application.\n\nIn this lesson, you will learn:\n- What happens when a user clicks a button in the browser\n- How requests travel from client to server\n- How servers process requests and send responses\n\n---\n\n## Key Concepts\n- HTTP and HTTPS protocols\n- Request methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)\n- Status codes and their meanings\n- JSON as a data exchange format\n\n---\n\n## Why it’s important\nUnderstanding client–server communication will help you debug API issues confidently, build scalable applications, and design clean and maintainable backend services.",
